@startuml
title 3.7.4 Upload claim evidence
caption UC-044 | Implemented
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor white
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
show footbox
<style>
lifeLine {
    LineStyle 0
}
</style>
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor white
    ActorBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBorderColor black
    GroupBackgroundColor white
    GroupHeaderBackgroundColor white
}

' Source: apps/api-node/src/modules/claims/application/claim.use-cases.ts
' Main entity migration: apps/api-node/src/migrations/002_lost_found_schema.sql
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Claimant / Finder" as Actor
participant "Private Conversation" as Page
participant "Claims API" as API
participant "Claim Chat Service" as Service
participant "claim_evidence" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Upload claim evidence
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: POST /api/claims/:id/evidence (multipart)
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Upload claim evidence
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Require consented active participant; validate PHOTO and image
Service -> Service: 6: Coordinate stable upload operation; check replay and authorization
Service -> Table: 7: SELECT upload-operation evidence reference
activate Table
Table --> Service: 8: Existing reference or upload context
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 9: Validate image bytes; save private asset through storage adapter
alt Asset storage succeeds
Service -> Service: 10: Persist reference with business recheck in coordinated transaction
Service -> Table: 11: INSERT PHOTO evidence with locked-room recheck
activate Table
Table --> Service: 12: Persistence acknowledgement / reference
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 13: Commit and reconcile operation on authoritative primary
alt Persistence confirmed
Service -> Service: 14: Return protected API URL, never raw storage reference
Service --> API: 15: Protected evidence metadata
API --> Page: 16: HTTP 201: Protected evidence metadata
Page --> Actor: 17: Show authorized result
else Outcome unresolved or acknowledgement lost
Service -> Service: 14.1: Keep asset and operation; reconcile later / stable retry
Service --> API: 14.2: Do not claim success or delete possibly referenced asset
API --> Page: 14.3: HTTP 503
Page --> Actor: 14.4: Display error; do not report success
end
else Storage unavailable
Service --> API: 10.1: No confirmed persisted upload
API --> Page: 10.2: HTTP 503
Page --> Actor: 10.3: Display error; do not report success
end
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 / 401 / 403 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Scope: Composer Evidence opens/focuses the upload form. Evidence is not an IMAGE chat message and
does not verify ownership. Uncertain DB writes retain assets.
endlegend
@enduml
